englishSenses.definition:
A vacuum tube in which the exhaustion is carried to a
   very high degree, with the production of a distinct class of effects;
   -- so called from W. Crookes who introduced it.

n. A contrivance used to supply small quantities of
   sweetened liquid, water, etc., to any mixture, or to test tubes, etc.;
   a dropping bottle.

plural of legalist
n. One who practices or advocates strict conformity to law;
   in theology, one who holds to the law of works. See Legal, 2 (a).
